    "native_visual_review_evidence": "RG041 G REGISTER BITS 04-07 — native author review\n\nSource: D:/Reference Materials/IBM 360/IBM_360_ALD/RG G Register/RG041 G REGISTER BITS 04-07.tif\nSHA256: 66b5b28c4779080622ce8ac928f5f4abd4c330cac2012d1d08c1447fc8db22b4\nOriginal scan filename: RG G Register/img20141205_21582050.tif\nOriginal order before: RG001 G REGISTER BITS 00-03.tif\nOriginal order after: RG051 G REGISTER P BIT AND CONTROLS.tif\n\nNative source and full preview comparison completed.\nStandard zero-based 245x103 grid; all banks remain [50,73,96,119,142,165,188]. Normal seven-row bodies, open bottoms, native grid/ID bottom spacing. Native rough calibration x=365+40*c, y=318+60*r reproduces multiple banks and ranks; minor scan skew is not interpreted as a block shift. Title frame is c210..241 / r93..102. Header and both vertical page references are RG041; bottom subpages are 000.\n\nEvery block, pin and printed field was read on this page, rather than inferred from RG001. The eight gates for each bit were reviewed in bit4/5/6/7 left.png and bit4/5/6/7 right.png. A1 cross-check confirms all32 card portions and physical sockets. The four OR fields are 3358A9,3358AA,3358AB,3358AC. Their unit is U03AE; their starred T output annotations remain printed. The four final driver units are S06CB, not 506CB.\n\nShared +SET G REG comes from RG051BD4 on r7, descends c44, and drives AA/AC/AE/AG.D04. Shared -RESET G REG comes from RG051BC4 on r10, descends c45, and drives AB/AD/AF/AH.B10. Each first three branches have a source diamond, and each last bottom bend is unjoined to the adjacent wire and has no invented diamond. The four latched SUM sources cross these rails without joining. Reviewed on source rails.png and shared rails full.png.\n\nEach latch AND pair feeds its native two unlabeled OR inputs. Each OR output drives its inverter and its upper AR buffer via the explicit diamond at c92. Each inverter output feeds its indicator and returns below the latch into the lower AND's B07/B12/D07/D12 input; the explicit c107 output diamond remains visible. Feedback-loop low rows are 19,40,61,82 and their c46 input corners are retained.\n\nEach upper AR has a separate positive output to the following inverter and a starred main output to BF601. Both printed wedges on each upper AR output and its input are retained. The following inverter and S06CB input are unlabeled plain outputs/inputs where printed. The S06CB driver prints two physical outputs: the main B02/D02/D13/B13 starred pin and lower KB03/KD11/KD10/KD09 pin at its bottom row. The main and lower pins join only at their short c200 native loop diamond; both physical pins share one same-block net driver. The K qualifiers are literal annotations retained in the drawing. Output borders are plain. Reviewed in output4/5/6/7.png.\n\nAll12 right destination lines and their final IDs were checked in right labels.png and output refs contact.png: WA291 +DIR OUT DATA BIT 04-07, BF601 - G REG BIT 04-07, KT041 -IND G REG 04-07. Their output names begin at211 and join their final IDs at242 through continuous wires. A blank before each leading sign follows the native reference.\n\nFooter checked against footer.png and connector table.png. Connector columns begin at34,48,62,76,90; rows94..102. AW4 continuation is 02A-D3A7B02: AW footer exact enlarged.png resolves B with two closed bowls. ECs are08-08-69 713380 and05-01-70 713674. Title G REGISTER BITS 04-07; DATE05-28-70; MACH.7201-02; LOG403; FRAME02; P.N.2585851; IBM CORP. SDD BLK.DM. P.N. periods are large native dots; no o is inferred. Machine and P.N. each leave the required blank at240 before the right border.\n\nFull draft preview was compared to the overview, then all eight per-bit native crops, four driver-output crops, source-rail crops and footer/connector crops. Font JuliaMono20, character width12, row height18, no wrapping; final preview2960x1874 pixels. All diamonds visible, no inferred joins at plain crossings, no pin labels detached from borders, no lower-case or disallowed diagram characters, no unreadable fields. Geometry checks confirm connected nets, one driver per input, no shared segments between different nets, no paths inside bodies and all terminals attached. Independent root comparison remains pending.\n",
